cyte densities frequently result in mosquito infection</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2007</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>470</fpage><lpage>474</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17360869</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Boudin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Olivier</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Molez</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chiron</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Ambroise-Thomas</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><article-title>High human malarial infectivity to laboratory-bred Anopheles gambiae in a village in Burkina Faso</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1993</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>700</fpage><lpage>706</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8517489</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Muirhead-Thomson</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><article-title>The malarial infectivity of an African village population to mosquitoes (Anopheles gambiae); a random xenodiagnostic survey</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1957</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>971</fpage><lpage>979</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13487967</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Felger</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanner</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Beck</surname><given-names>HP</given-names></name><article-title>Premunition in Plasmodium falciparum infection: insights from the epidemiology of multiple infections</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1999</year><volume>93</volume><issue>Suppl 1</issue><fpage>59</fpage><lpage>64</lpage><pub-id pub-id-ty